Z||000002||overlord||02-11-2001||10:31 AM||||speaking of cold....<BR>Drove home from work the other morning and it  was  -36C.<P>-seat was like a rock<BR>-headlights had trouble going up<BR>-frozen brakes<BR>-trunk frozen up wouldnt open<BR>-had trouble keeping it running when first started.<BR>-and to top it off....car was overheating by the time i was halfway home...and leaking something. (hose probably cracked from the cold I HOPE).   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||02-12-2001||01:57 AM||||Sounds like your coolant froze up.  My GT did that a few times earlier this year when it hitting -15 and -20*f here.  Didn't burst anything and even survived a 15 mile drive.. at the redline and steaming a little when I got home but didn't break anything.  Sounds like you probably did crack a hose.   After it warmed up a bit I drained about a gallon of coolant and added straight antifreeze.  Haven't had a problem since.||||reg||1
